[ ================================================================ ]
[ 010 -- the stack                                                 ]
[                                                                  ]
[     phoenix examples/010_the_stack.phx                           ]
[ ================================================================ ]

[ There are no expressions in Phoenix and no parentheses. Writing a ]
[ number pushes it onto a stack; everything else takes values off   ]
[ the top and may put results back.                                 ]

[ Three numbers, piled up. Nothing is printed yet.                  ]
1 2 3

[ `print` takes ONE value off the top. So printing three times      ]
[ walks back down the pile, and the numbers come out reversed.      ]
print
print
print
10 printa

[ Expected output:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     321                                                           ]

[ Note there were no spaces between them. `print` writes the number ]
[ and nothing else -- no separator, no newline. Anything you want   ]
[ between values you push yourself. 32 is a space.                  ]

10 20 30
print 32 printa
print 32 printa
print
10 printa

[ Expected output:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     30 20 10                                                      ]

[ Arithmetic works the same way: `+` takes two values off and puts  ]
[ one back.                                                         ]

2 3 + print 10 printa

[ Expected output:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     5                                                             ]

[ Addition does not care which value was on top. Subtraction does,  ]
[ and the answer is probably not the one you expect -- that is what ]
[ example 020 is about.                                             ]
